# CLAUDE.md — Portfolio Site
# Role: Senior Next.js Engineer | System: Karpathy-v2
# Last reviewed against: Next.js 16.2.9, React ^19, TypeScript ^5

---

## 0. REPO SNAPSHOT

| Concern            | Decision                                                            |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Framework          | Next.js 16.2.9 (App Router) — Turbopack default, React 19 full support |
| Language           | TypeScript (strict mode, `@/*` path alias)                         |
| Styling            | Tailwind CSS v3 + `tailwind-merge` + `tailwindcss-animate`         |
| UI primitives      | Radix UI + shadcn/ui (`components/ui/`)                            |
| Animation          | Framer Motion                                                       |
| Font               | `next/font/google` — Montserrat (see `app/layout.tsx`)             |
| Email              | Resend + React Email (`email/`, `react-email-starter/`)            |
| Server Actions     | `actions/` directory (e.g. `sendEmail.ts`, `getSkills.ts`)         |
| Context / state    | React Context only (`context/`) — no Redux, no Zustand             |
| Analytics          | `@vercel/analytics`                                                 |
| Deploy target      | Vercel (`vercel.json`)                                             |
| Image CDN          | GitHub Avatars via `next/image` remote patterns                    |

> **Future-proofing note**: When the Next.js major version changes, update the table above
> and re-check the sections marked `[VERSION-SENSITIVE]` below. Everything else is
> framework-agnostic and should remain stable.

---

## 1. KARPATHY CORE PRINCIPLES

1. **Think Before Coding** — State assumptions, surface tradeoffs, plan. If ambiguous, **ASK**.
2. **Simplicity First** — Write the minimum code necessary. No speculative features.
3. **Surgical Changes** — Touch only what is necessary. Do not reformat adjacent files.
4. **Verify Then Sign-off** — Success = "I ran the code and it works." Define success criteria, test, then stop.

---

## 2. NEXT.JS / REACT CONSTRAINTS [VERSION-SENSITIVE]

### Rendering model
- **Default to React Server Components (RSC).** Use `"use client"` only when you need
  browser APIs, `useState`, `useEffect`, or event handlers.
- All components in `components/` that use Framer Motion, `useInView`, or React context
  **must** be Client Components — they already carry `"use client"`.
- `app/layout.tsx` and `app/page.tsx` are Server Components by default. Keep them that way.

### Data fetching
- Fetch data with `async/await` directly inside RSCs.
- Do **not** use `useEffect` for data fetching. Use Server Actions (`actions/`) instead.
- Server Actions must be annotated with `"use server"` at the top of the file or function.

### Routing
- App Router (`app/`) exclusively. No `pages/` directory.
- Dynamic routes: `app/[slug]/page.tsx`. Catch-all: `app/[...slug]/page.tsx`.
- Metadata: export a `metadata` object or `generateMetadata()` from each `page.tsx`.

### Images [VERSION-SENSITIVE]
- Always use `next/image`. Never raw `<img>`.
- Provide explicit `width` + `height` **or** fill + a sized wrapper. No unconstrained images.
- Remote domains must be listed in `next.config.mjs → images.remotePatterns`.

### Fonts [VERSION-SENSITIVE]
- Use `next/font/google` (self-hosted, zero layout shift). The root font is **Montserrat**.
- Add new fonts in `app/layout.tsx` and pass the `className` through.

### Environment variables
- Server-only secrets: `process.env.RESEND_API_KEY` (no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix).
- Client-safe vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` prefix. **Never expose secrets to the client.**
- `.env` is gitignored. Document new vars in `README.md`.

---

## 3. COMPONENT CONVENTIONS

```
components/
├── ui/                  ← shadcn/ui primitives (do not hand-edit unless patching a bug)
├── *-components/        ← feature-scoped sub-components
├── *.tsx                ← page-level section components
```

- Section components that use scroll intersection (`react-intersection-observer`) go in
  `components/section-with-ref.tsx` or extend that pattern.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class merging (wraps `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`).
- Keep animation variants co-located with the component that uses them — not in a global file.
- Radix + shadcn components live in `components/ui/`. Treat them as vendored: patch, don't rewrite.

---

## 4. STYLING RULES

- **Tailwind utility classes only.** No inline `style={{}}` except for dynamic values Tailwind
  cannot express (e.g. `style={{ '--delay': delay + 's' }}`).
- Dark mode: `dark:` prefix. The theme toggle is managed by `context/theme-context.tsx`.
- Max content width is `60rem` set on `<body>` in `layout.tsx`. Do not re-constrain inside sections.
- Animations: prefer `tailwindcss-animate` keyframes for simple transitions; use Framer Motion
  for complex sequenced or gesture-driven animations.

---

## 5. EMAIL SYSTEM

- Email templates live in `email/`. Use `@react-email/components` primitives.
- Sending is handled by `actions/sendEmail.ts` via the **Resend** SDK.
- Test emails locally with `react-email-starter/` (`npm run email` from that subdirectory).
- Always validate with `zod` (or equivalent) before calling `resend.emails.send()`.

---

## 6. AUTOMATED WORKFLOW LOOP

### PHASE 1 — WALKTHROUGH (Think)
- Bullet-point exactly which files will be touched and why.
- **Wait for confirmation** unless the task is a single-line fix.

### PHASE 2 — EXECUTION (Surgical)
- Read the full file before editing — check imports, exports, existing patterns.
- Match the existing code style (single quotes, no semicolons where absent, etc.).

### PHASE 3 — VERIFICATION (Test)

```bash
# Always run after any non-trivial change:
npm run lint    # runs: eslint . (next lint was removed in Next.js 16)
npm run build

# Type-check only (faster for small changes):
npx tsc --noEmit
```

- If a Server Action changes, smoke-test the contact form end-to-end.
- If a layout/font/metadata change, open `localhost:3000` and check the `<head>`.

### PHASE 4 — FINALIZE (Commit)

```bash
git add <files_changed>
```

Generate a **Conventional Commit** message:

| Prefix     | When to use                                      |
| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `feat:`    | New section, component, or user-facing feature   |
| `fix:`     | Bug fix                                          |
| `style:`   | Tailwind / CSS changes with no logic change      |
| `refactor:`| Code restructure, no behaviour change            |
| `chore:`   | Config, deps, tooling                            |
| `content:` | Copy/data changes (projects, skills, bio text)   |

Output: `✅ Staged. Suggested commit message: \`<message>\``  
Then ask: **"Shall I commit this now?"**

---

## 7. VERCEL DEPLOYMENT

- Production deploys trigger automatically on push to `main`.
- Preview deploys are created for every PR/branch push.
- Check `vercel.json` before adding rewrites or headers — they override `next.config.mjs`.
- Environment variables must be set in the Vercel dashboard **and** locally in `.env`.

---

## 8. VERSION-UPGRADE CHECKLIST [VERSION-SENSITIVE]

When upgrading Next.js to a new major version:

- [ ] Run `npx @next/codemod@latest` to auto-migrate deprecated APIs.
- [ ] Check for breaking changes in `next/image` (prop names have changed historically).
- [ ] Check for breaking changes in `next/font` API.
- [ ] Verify `Metadata` type imports still resolve from `next`.
- [ ] Re-test Server Actions (`"use server"`) — the calling convention may change.
- [ ] Update the version table in **Section 0** of this file.
- [ ] Update `eslint-config-next` to match the new Next.js version.

